Chromium: keep kCrossDeviceSignin/kCrossDeviceSigninUrl Android/iOS only.

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.
Source: Chromium electron-source tree under EmberBSD, after the
chromium-nb (NetBSD) patch set.

The chromium-nb overlay widens the Android/iOS block in
signin_switches.cc with IS_BSD, but the matching declarations in
signin_switches.h stay Android/iOS only and nothing on desktop BSD
uses them (desktop uses kCrossDeviceSigninFromDesktop). The definition
then has internal linkage and clang reports
-Wunused-const-variable under -Werror. Restore the guard to match the
header instead of silencing the diagnostic.

--- a/components/signin/public/base/signin_switches.cc
+++ b/components/signin/public/base/signin_switches.cc
@@ -267,7 +267,7 @@
              base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
 
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS) || BUILDFLAG(IS_BSD)
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS)
 BASE_FEATURE(kCrossDeviceSignin, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 const base::FeatureParam<std::string> kCrossDeviceSigninUrl{&kCrossDeviceSignin,
                                                             "url", ""};
